  "faten": "مس فاتن",
  "layan": "ليان"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Still dealing with the fallout at AlRawabi School, Principal Ms. Faten lectures the students on honesty and responsibility and asks for witnesses. Layan steps forward with her friends to corner Mariam. Listen to the whole scene in Jordanian Arabic first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "المدرسة صارت كابوس إلي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أهم القيم عنا هون بمدرسة الروابي واضحة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لازم نتحمل المسؤولية ونحكي الصدق.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بظن صار الوقت نحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أي حدا منكم شاف اللي صار؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "نعم يا مس، أنا شفت كل إشي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "وصحباتي كمان شافوا اللي صار.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "لا يا مس، ليان ما بتحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "الغرفة مليانة بنات يا مريم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وكلهم شهدوا على إشي واحد.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وإنتي بدك أصدقك لحالك؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "أنا بحكي الصدق بس ما حدا سامعني.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's slow down and look at each line one by one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "المدرسة صارت كابوس إلي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'School became a nightmare for me.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "صارت",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"she became\", matching \"school\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "كابوس",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the Arabic word for a nightmare.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أهم القيم عنا هون بمدرسة الروابي واضحة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The most important values we have here at AlRawabi School are clear.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أهم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"most important\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "عنا هون",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is smooth Jordanian speech for \"we have here\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لازم نتحمل المسؤولية ونحكي الصدق.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We must take responsibility and tell the truth.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لازم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is an unchangeable helper word meaning \"must\"—you never have to alter its shape no matter who speaks.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بظن صار الوقت نحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I think it is time we tell the truth.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بظن",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"I think\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "صار الوقت",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally says \"the time became\", which is how Arabic says \"it's time\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أي حدا منكم شاف اللي صار؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did any one of you see what happened?' Notice ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "اللي صار",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " at the end: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "اللي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"that which\" or \"what\", so ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "اللي صار",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"what happened\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "نعم يا مس، أنا شفت كل إشي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes Miss, I saw everything.' Layan uses polite ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "نعم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " with the principal, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "شفت",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from شاف, the everyday Levantine word for seeing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "وصحباتي كمان شافوا اللي صار.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And my friends also saw what happened.' Drop ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "كمان",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " into almost any sentence when you want to say \"also\", \"too\", or \"even more\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "لا يا مس، ليان ما بتحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No Miss, Layan is not telling the truth.' Putting ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ما",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " right before ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بتحكي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " flips \"she speaks\" into \"she does not speak\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "الغرفة مليانة بنات يا مريم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The room is full of girls, Mariam.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "مليانة",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"full\", built from the root for filling something to the brim.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وكلهم شهدوا على إشي واحد.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And all of them testified to one thing.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "كلهم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " glues \"all\" and \"them\" into a single word, a pattern Arabic uses constantly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وإنتي بدك أصدقك لحالك؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And you want me to believe you alone?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بدك",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"you want\" when speaking to a woman, while ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لحالك",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally says \"by your own state\" for \"all alone\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "أنا بحكي الصدق بس ما حدا سامعني.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am telling the truth, only nobody hears me.' Pairing ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ما",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "حدا",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " gives \"nobody\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "سامعني",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " tacks \"me\" straight onto the end of \"hearing\". Now let's listen to the whole exchange again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "المدرسة صارت كابوس إلي.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أهم القيم عنا هون بمدرسة الروابي واضحة.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لازم نتحمل المسؤولية ونحكي الصدق.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بظن صار الوقت نحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "أي حدا منكم شاف اللي صار؟",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "نعم يا مس، أنا شفت كل إشي.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "وصحباتي كمان شافوا اللي صار.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "لا يا مس، ليان ما بتحكي الحقيقة.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "الغرفة مليانة بنات يا مريم.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وكلهم شهدوا على إشي واحد.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وإنتي بدك أصدقك لحالك؟",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "أنا بحكي الصدق بس ما حدا سامعني.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Outnumbered by false witnesses, Mariam sees her favorite place turn against her. Notice how كمان for \"also\" and حدا for \"anyone\" pop up naturally throughout the conversation. See you next time.",
   "gap": 0.5
